  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pos100-1700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Pos 1501.06 Eligibility",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pos 1501.06 Eligibility. An applicant for tuition repayment under this program shall:\n\n(a) Complete and submit the application for CART/sign language interpreter tuition repayment (PEC-CART);\n\n(b) Be employed, or self-employed, and work at least 30 hours per week, on average, as a CART provider or sign language interpreter in New Hampshire for the prior 12 months;\n\n(c) Have certification/licensure as specified in Pos 1501.03;\n\n(d) Show evidence, through the submission of a completed application, that he or she has completed one year of service in New Hampshire for each year of tuition repayment; and\n\n(e) Submit the application by the deadline.\n\nSource. #9677, eff 3-13-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pos100-1700.html"
